WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

NOTE Synthetic lecture fixture for the locator spike. Chapters: 00:00 Intro, 00:01:10 Gradient descent, 00:02:30 Learning rate.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Welcome back. Today we look at how a model
learns from its mistakes.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:14.000
The loss function measures how wrong the
predictions are on the training data.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Keep that picture of a loss surface in mind.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:19.250
Gradient descent takes a step in the direction
that lowers the loss the fastest.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:27.000
That direction is the negative of the gradient.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:41.000
The learning rate sets the size of each step.
Too large and training diverges.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Too small and training crawls along for ages.

01:02:03.040 --> 01:02:09.000
<v Lecturer>That is all for today, see you next week.
